        Standards are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0, and
        their code examples under the MIT license. CERT and Carnegie Mellon
        are registered trademarks of Carnegie Mellon University.
    description:
        The Software Engineering Institute's secure coding rules for C, each
        aimed at a class of undefined behavior or exploitable defect. Every
        rule carries a risk assessment of severity, likelihood and priority.
